// A link that leaves the drawing still gets a page to be drawn on.
//
// A link's geometry is measured off the solved layout rather than solved for,
// so the resolver sizes the canvas from the boxes alone and knows nothing about
// where the lines go. A curve out of a `top` side arches above every box in the
// drawing, and its label rides higher still; both used to be clipped in silence.
// The renderer grows the page around whatever it draws instead.
//
// The cases here: an arch over the widest gap in the file, one over the
// narrowest, a loop off the left of the leftmost box, and one dipping under the
// lowest — the boxes cover 378x230 and the page has grown to 428x312 to hold
// what the lines do outside that.

diagram background: #111111

style box  fill: #191728  border: #4f5367

box a "A"                            style: box
box b "B"  right of a  (gap: wide)   style: box
box c "C"  right of b                style: box

box d "D"  below a and c             style: box

// The long arch. Its handles reach their limit, so the curve rises well clear
// of the boxes and the label sits at the top of it.
link a -> b  "over the top"  from: top  to: top

// The same shape across a narrow gap: a smaller arch, still above the boxes.
link b -> c  from: top  to: top

// Out of the left of the leftmost box and back into the bottom of it, which
// puts the whole loop off the left-hand edge of what the boxes cover.
link d -> a  "round the side"  from: left  to: left

// And below the bottom row.
link a -> d  from: bottom  to: bottom
